// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// client/src/translations/phrases.js
//
// The rest of the floor's text, by phrase: [English, Afrikaans, isiXhosa].
//
// messages.js holds the text that screens ask for by key (home, the tab
// bar, Packing). Everything else on the floor is written in English in
// its own component, and is translated on the page by floorTranslator.js
// from this table: the English is looked up exactly as it is shown.
//
// TO ADD OR FIX A LINE: the first entry must match the English on the
// screen exactly, including punctuation and the kind of apostrophe.
// {} stands for something filled in (a number, a name, a date); it is
// carried across in the same order.
//
// A line that is not here stays in English. To see what is missing,
// run  localStorage.setItem('wms_i18n_debug', '1')  in the browser,
// reload, walk the screens, then read  window.__wmsUntranslated.
//
// LIKE messages.js, THE AFRIKAANS AND ISIXHOSA ARE DRAFTS AND HAVE NOT
// BEEN CHECKED BY A FLUENT SPEAKER. Names of products, centres, people
// and suppliers are data and must not be added here.
//
// Loaded only when a language other than English is chosen.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

